abstract: >
  Public web calculator implementing Cox proportional hazards models for prediction of
  Event-Free Survival (EFS = relapse OR progression) at 12 and 24 months after the
  mid-treatment timepoint (CXJ1), using circulating tumor DNA (ctDNA) minimal residual
  disease (MRD) markers in adult B-cell lymphomas and classical Hodgkin lymphoma.

  V230.4 (May 2026) introduces histology-specific v5A driver panels (Hodgkin 16
  genes / Non-Hodgkin 16 genes) selected by exhaustive backward elimination, after
  blacklisting genes with HR<1 or p>0.5 univariate per histology and excluding Ig
  V(D)J genes. The model combines four covariates per pipeline variant (kinetic
  score, log baseline tumor burden, panel signal, Deauville interim PET) and uses
  partial pooling between IDES (MOABI hybrid-capture) and PV (phased-variant UMI)
  pipelines with strata histology × pipeline. Bootstrap optimism-corrected C-index
  on the optimal stacked variant (M2 hEq Deauv, N=230, 42 events): 0.862.
